            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "It’s intentional, when it’s nil it means the buffer is empty or the file isn’t being used, and also if the file wasn’t under git when it was opened in Neovim it will stay nil even if you add a `.git` later while it’s still open.\r\nThe solution is to restart Neovim, for example using `:restart`, or just reopen it.\r\nPlease don’t use AI :/\r\n\r\n",
