            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> 2\\. **No re-attach loop is possible.** `auto_enable` is gated on `H.is_buf_enabled(buf_id)` and fires only on `BufEnter`. After `fail_attach`, `H.cache[buf_id]` is `nil` (buffer disabled); nothing schedules another enable until the user switches to the buffer again — which is exactly when a retry is wanted (the user may have just run `git init`).\r\n\r\nRetry on user switching to the buffer again is *exactly* when trying to re-attach is not wanted. Because it will lead to unlimited re-attach tries for files that are not in the Git repository.\r\n\r\n> The solution is to restart Neovim, for example using `:restart`, or just reopen it.\r\n\r\nAlthough this would work, the intended solution is to explicitly `:edit` in the file. This causes detach and the re-attach. However, this works in 'mini.git' but not in 'mini.diff'. I'll take a look, this should be more or less straightforward.\r\n\r\nBut this PR is definitely not the wanted approach, sorry.",
